 - Signed amounts: expenses negative, income positive. Normalize on import.
 - New Rust command → register in `invoke_handler!`, add a `dispatch` arm in `server.rs` (+ `COMMANDS` entry), add wrapper in `api.ts`. The `dispatch_parity_with_tauri_commands` test guards the list.
 - Commits are logical work groups: one concern per commit, only the files that belong to it. Never sweep another session's in-flight edits into your commit — leave foreign changes unstaged in the working tree.
+- Worktrees live in `.worktrees/` (gitignored, inside the project so no per-session permission prompts): `git worktree add .worktrees/<name> -b <branch> <base>`. Do feature work there; keep the main checkout clean.
+- `.worktrees/` is excluded from every scanner — git, eslint, prettier, the Vite watcher, svelte-check/tsconfig (root-scoped `src/` globs), Storybook (`../src/**`), Playwright (`tests/`), pytest (`testpaths`), ruff/rg/`zg`/GitNexus (all respect `.gitignore`; verified 0 worktree files in the GitNexus index). Adding a new scanner/linter/indexer? Give it the same exclusion before its first run.
+- In PyCharm: Mark Directory as → Excluded on `.worktrees/` so the IDE doesn't double-index nested checkouts. Never run `prettier --write .`, `eslint --fix .`, or `npm run index` expecting them to cross into (or from) a worktree — each checkout lints and indexes itself.
 - Python: managed with uv (`uv sync --extra pandas`); run scripts via `uv run python …`. Scripts stay pure stdlib unless justified; pandas optional with fallback.
 - SQLite lives in OS app-data dir (`monartha.db`, adopted from legacy `myfinances.db` on first run); dev fallback `./data/`.
 - Verify before finishing: `cargo check`, `npm run check`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build`.
